<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gordian II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 192–238</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gordian II was Roman emperor for about three weeks in 238, jointly with his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gordian-i">Gordian I</a>. When a revolt at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/el-djem">Thysdrus</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a> proclaimed the elderly proconsul emperor against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maximinus-thrax">Maximinus Thrax</a>, the Senate recognised both. Gordian II was killed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carthage">Carthage</a> fighting the Numidian legion under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/capelianus">Capelianus</a>, and his father hanged himself; his nephew later reigned as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gordian-iii">Gordian III</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gordian-ii.jpg" alt="Gordian II" width="320" height="331" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Gordiano_II_-_ritratto_da_sesterzio.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
